# PATCH CONTEXT
# Why: RN 0.87 no longer provides CallInvoker or CallbackWrapper transitively,
#   and Expo 54's Objective-C delegate wrapper imports a generated Swift header
#   across pod boundaries. Expo's current source owns a finite Objective-C
#   protocol for that Swift delegate instead. RN's Android AAR also omits the
#   jserrorhandler header required by its deprecated cxxreact forwarding header.
#   Expo's bridgeless JSI setup must also read RN 0.87's RuntimeExecutor directly
#   from ReactContext instead of constructing the deprecated CatalystInstance.
# Remove when: Expo Modules Core includes both JSI owner headers, exposes its
#   React delegate through EXReactDelegateProtocol, and supports RN 0.87's
#   ErrorUtils header layout and direct bridgeless RuntimeExecutor API.

